## Errors & Mistakes
- The first renders showed a frozen second copy of the board during every camera move. Scene.get_moving_and_static_mobjects flattens families in begin_animations, so the Stage polygons from the first frame of each play() were drawn on every frame. The fix overrides it to return list(self.mobjects).
- Several callouts that pointed right were cropped at the frame edge. In the template, two callouts overlapped ("Compute die" and "Memory stacks"). Both were fixed by pointing labels left or down.
- On this Mac, stat is GNU stat from coreutils gnubin, so `stat -f "%m %z"` printed filesystem information instead of the file's mtime.
- A python heredoc followed by `rm render.sh && ls` hung until the 2-minute timeout, although both had already run. I killed the shell. The cause is unknown.
- engine.py first defined BLUE and ORANGE, which shadow Manim's colors of the same names. Replaced them with the ACCENT dict before this commit.
- The first draft of this commit message had a body line that started with "Manim:". commitlint parsed it as a footer (footer-leading-blank warning).

