## Hints for Future Agents
- render.sh writes VIDEO.mp4 beside the module only at QUALITY=h. Drafts go to MEDIA_DIR.
- Each video keeps its own copy of engine.py on purpose. Do not refactor a video to import the engine from the skill directory.
- Each scene must end in the next scene's START. Keep looping pulses off screen at a seam, and do not use hash() for phases (it changes per process).
- render() is exact only for boxes that do not intersect. Grow a part that splits into layers only after it has lifted clear of its neighbors.
- Pango cannot see SF Pro, so the engine uses Helvetica Neue. A Text with "\n" leaves large gaps between lines, so use headline() and body().
- PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 in render.sh and sys.dont_write_bytecode in preview.py keep __pycache__ out of video folders.

## Codebase Discoveries
- installers/install-skills.sh links skills/* into ~/.claude/skills and ~/.agents/skills, then deletes every broken symlink directly under those folders, including links that dotfiles did not create.
- The other skills resolve SKILL_DIR by reading the link of ~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md. This skill uses the same pattern.

